\f0\fs24 \cf2 Fausto's bedroom has remained almost intact, but if you look closely, you'll notice some differences. Once, there was a large rug beneath the bed, and the walls were covered with wallpaper that added warmth to the room. Over time, however, those fabrics deteriorated and were removed. But look at the rest: the armchair, the bed, and that magnificent polyptych by Giampietrino (a student of Leonardo) are still there, just as Fausto and Giuseppe had arranged them. It\'92s as if time has stood still, and who knows, perhaps one day we\'92ll see a new wallpaper recreated from archival photos. Maybe even the rug under the bed will return to its former glory.\
